00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:39,375
<i>♪ On that wretched isle ♪</i>

498
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:41,252
<i>♪ Cast aside, doing time ♪</i>

499
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:43,046
<i>♪ Pushed me over the edge ♪</i>

500
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:46,799
<i>♪ But the way you beg and plead
is bringing back my smile ♪</i>

501
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:51,262
<i>♪ Understand Wonderland's
gonna feel my revenge ♪</i>

502
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:53,097
<i>- ♪ You're heartless ♪
- ♪ You mean it? ♪</i>

503
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,182
You monster!

504
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,266
Believe it.

505
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,310
You'll never get away with this!

506
00:23:57,311 --> 00:23:59,854
<i>♪ I already have ♪</i>

507
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:02,065
<i>♪ Welcome to my Wonderland ♪</i>

508
00:24:02,066 --> 00:24:04,359
<i>♪ To my Wonderland ♪</i>

509
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,527
<i>♪ Truth or dare
Are you scared? ♪</i>

510
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:07,654
<i>♪ That's too bad ♪</i>

511
00:24:07,655 --> 00:24:09,781
<i>♪ Welcome to my Wonderland ♪</i>

512
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:11,617
<i>♪ It's better than I planned ♪</i>

513
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:16,496
<i>♪ What a time
Most fun I've ever had ♪</i>

514
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:18,623
<i>♪ I've never been so happy being ♪</i>

515
00:24:18,624 --> 00:24:20,541
<i>♪ Criminal beyond all reason ♪</i>

516
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:22,627
<i>♪ Never been so happy being ♪</i>

517
00:24:22,628 --> 00:24:24,128
- Wait!
<i>- ♪ Mad! ♪</i>

518
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:29,550
You're getting fingerprints on my crystal!

519
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:31,637
I will find your vault.

520
00:24:32,638 --> 00:24:36,683
How long your rescuers suffer until I do
is up to you.

521
00:24:36,684 --> 00:24:39,978
You underestimate my girls.

522
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:41,647
You underestimate...

523
00:24:42,815 --> 00:24:43,940
me.

524
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,453
And stay out.

525
00:24:57,454 --> 00:24:59,247
What was that?

526
00:24:59,248 --> 00:25:01,332
Well, I'm partial to <i>"gracias,"</i>

527
00:25:01,333 --> 00:25:03,293
but, uh, "thank you" also works,

528
00:25:04,086 --> 00:25:06,713
you know, for saving you.

529
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:09,258
Does it look like we're saved?

530
00:25:10,426 --> 00:25:12,928
Wait, where is everybody?

531
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:19,518
Probably behind door number one,
two or... seven ninety-four.

532
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,770
But, hey, this is your backyard, right?

533
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:25,107
So, uh, which one do we start with?

534
00:25:26,442 --> 00:25:27,942
I wish I knew.

535
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:29,277
What was that?

536
00:25:29,278 --> 00:25:30,696
Let's go with this one.

537
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:33,990
Uh, this one's the one.

538
00:25:33,991 --> 00:25:35,658
- Yeah.
- Lead the way.

539
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:37,076
I'm sure everybody's fine.

540
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:42,540
Whoa!

541
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:43,667
Get off me!

542
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:46,545
Whoa!

543
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:48,921
Looks like a fun guy.

544
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:54,887
-  No luck?
- Let's keep going.

545
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,682
They've got to be around here somewhere.

546
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:01,977
Ugh! What?

547
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,730
Are you sure you're going the right way?

548
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,940
I'm walking this way, aren't I?

549
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:11,945
How does one get lost
in their own kingdom, exactly?

550
00:26:13,155 --> 00:26:14,490
Fine.

551
00:26:15,199 --> 00:26:16,783
You got me. Okay?

552
00:26:16,784 --> 00:26:18,117
I don't like bows.

553
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:19,619
I prefer swords to sparkles.

554
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:21,829
And this isn't my backyard.

555
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:23,039
- I didn't--
- You try being

556
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:25,500
shut off from the world your whole life,

557
00:26:25,501 --> 00:26:28,586
and the minute you get
a whiff of fresh air, you screw it up.

558
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:31,882
Not just for yourself,
but for everyone you've ever cared about.

559
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:37,178
- I didn't mean it like that.
- It's okay.

560
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:38,263
I get it.

561
00:26:40,057 --> 00:26:43,060
Trust me. I...
I know a thing or two about family legacy,

562
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:48,689
a blessing and a curse
all wrapped up together.

563
00:26:48,690 --> 00:26:50,108
I'm Louisa Madrigal's son.

564
00:26:50,109 --> 00:26:52,444
I'm supposed to be strong, no matter what.

565
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:55,447
Good thing I can, uh, shoulder it.

566
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,493
You gotta chill with all that.

567
00:27:00,494 --> 00:27:02,078
It's too much.

568
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:05,332
Sorry. It's kind of what people expect.

569
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:07,917
What they want from me.

570
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:09,920
All they seem to want from me.

571
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:12,965
Okay, but...

572
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:15,175
What do you want for you?

573
00:27:18,846 --> 00:27:21,723
I don't think anyone's
ever asked me that before.

574
00:27:26,895 --> 00:27:30,148
You know, now, I think
it's the part where you

575
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:34,068
apologize for dragging me
out of a doorway.

576
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:35,778
What?

577
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:38,115
- But I saved you.
- I can't with you.

578
00:27:38,824 --> 00:27:41,325
Is there an update
from Uma or the council?

579
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:44,538
Yes.
News from Fairy Godmother, Your Majesty.

580
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:50,793
The children have
gone to Wonderland... on their own?

581
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:53,714
Now they'll have to face Maddox alone.

582
00:27:54,715 --> 00:27:56,466
Chloe, what have you done?

583
00:28:02,389 --> 00:28:03,640
Smee!

584
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:07,895
Ha!

585
00:28:08,604 --> 00:28:10,771
See? Not lost after all.

586
00:28:11,899 --> 00:28:13,400
Smee!

587
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:16,862
Red! I was so worried!

588
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:19,280
You found it! Thank you!

589
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:20,656
Oh, I missed you, shoe.

590
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:21,949
Guys, Red found my shoe!

591
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:23,659
She is a ridiculous person.

592
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,162
Well, we've got a bigger problem.

593
00:28:26,330 --> 00:28:30,374
Whoa! Look, I'm not a fan
of Hazel's either, but let's pull it back.

594
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:32,252
No, it's not that. It's that.

595
00:28:32,878 --> 00:28:34,629
I saw one in the croquet garden.

596
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:36,589
It must be a spy for Maddox.

597
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:39,675
- So that's how he discovered us?
- Exactly.

598
00:28:39,676 --> 00:28:41,928
But listen, if we get the dodo down,

599
00:28:41,929 --> 00:28:44,555
maybe I can pry it open and rewire it,

600
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,307
and then it could spy for us

601
00:28:46,308 --> 00:28:48,059
so we can stay one step ahead of Maddox

602
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:50,144
and get
to the palace quicker to save your mom.

603
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,520
We should tell Max.

604
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:52,855
He might know more about them.

605
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,690
But, Red, listen.

606
00:28:54,691 --> 00:28:56,943
-  You tricked us.
-  I was trying to help.

607
00:28:56,944 --> 00:28:59,153
You like to box?
'Cause I got a killer right hook.

608
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:02,031
Even you can't think it's a coincidence
he led us to that madhouse.

609
00:29:02,032 --> 00:29:06,036
Guys, before someone gets a nose ring
they didn't consent to, look.

610
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,413
Is it one of your dad's?

611
00:29:09,331 --> 00:29:11,707
Looks like it.
And they'll have a direct line to him.

612
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:13,960
- We gotta destroy it.
- Or we can try to use it.

613
00:29:13,961 --> 00:29:15,169
No, he's right.

614
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:16,837
- It's too risky to mess with.
- But--

615
00:29:16,838 --> 00:29:18,798
- I'm on it, Red.
- Wait, Luis.

616
00:29:18,799 --> 00:29:20,926
I got it.

617
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:24,136
Get a clue you're extinct.

618
00:29:25,472 --> 00:29:28,350
Do you have a brain,
or are you just one big bicep?

619
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:30,935
Smees, get to climbing.

620
00:29:30,936 --> 00:29:32,103
Hey, put your hands up.

621
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:33,688
- Come on, make it good, make it good.
- Here I come.

622
00:29:33,689 --> 00:29:35,439
Not each other!

623
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:37,942
- The tree!
- Maybe we can lure it with treats.

624
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:39,485
It's a mechanical bird.

625
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:41,946
Yeah, but it's vanilla.
Everyone loves vanilla.

626
00:29:41,947 --> 00:29:45,282
No, I think if we just think enough--

627
00:29:45,283 --> 00:29:46,826
Yeah.

628
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,786
I think it's calling for more dodos.

629
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:50,079
Guys, we should keep moving.

630
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,330
Let's cover our tracks. Come on.

631
00:29:54,835 --> 00:29:55,919
Are you coming?

632
00:29:58,088 --> 00:29:59,297
Yeah, coming.

633
00:29:59,965 --> 00:30:01,882
Wait. Where's Robbie?

634
00:30:01,883 --> 00:30:03,009
I thought he was with you.

635
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,802
And Felix. I thought he was with you.

636
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:13,770
I hate this ride!

637
00:30:14,688 --> 00:30:15,897
Eh.

638
00:30:20,694 --> 00:30:23,654
These kids
are more resilient than I thought.

639
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:26,699
Chessy,
you cannot let them reach the palace.

640
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:30,537
I'm on it. This is something
I can really dig my claws into.

641
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,041
<i>Madam, it's too dangerous.</i>

642
00:30:35,042 --> 00:30:37,126
I haven't used it in years,

643
00:30:37,127 --> 00:30:39,837
but it leads directly
to Bridget's throne room.

644
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,256
Your Majesty doesn't know
what waits for her in there.

645
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:45,301
The Council is taking too long
and Chloe's in real danger.

646
00:30:45,302 --> 00:30:47,679
Find the king and send word
to Fairy Godmother.

647
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:50,932
It's time to be brave like my daughter.

648
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:58,523
Oh, my. Hello?

649
00:31:02,277 --> 00:31:03,445
Come on, old friend.

650
00:31:05,989 --> 00:31:06,990
I'm coming, Chloe.

651
00:31:09,034 --> 00:31:10,118
But not like this.

652
00:31:16,792 --> 00:31:18,417
- Bridget!
- Ella?

653
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:19,419
Ella!

654
00:31:22,089 --> 00:31:23,590
Whoo! That felt good.

655
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:28,344
Say what you will about
your stepmother's parenting,

656
00:31:28,345 --> 00:31:30,930
but you can sure
handle yourself with a broom.

657
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:32,556
- Are you hurt?
- Oh!

658
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:33,725
Are you all right?

659
00:31:34,392 --> 00:31:35,644
Are you wearing trousers?

660
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:37,895
Okay, you're fine.

661
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,106
Bridget, the girls are here in Wonderland.

662
00:31:40,107 --> 00:31:41,315
They came to rescue you.

663
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:42,858
We have to get them to safety.

664
00:31:42,859 --> 00:31:45,861
I know, but he
bewitched my throne room. I'm locked in.

665
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:48,239
I wasn't expecting visitors.

666
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,616
I didn't get your RSVP.

667
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:51,618
Maddox.

668
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:53,786
Cinderella.

669
00:31:53,787 --> 00:31:56,373
- She went in alone?
- I couldn't convince her to wait.

670
00:31:58,166 --> 00:31:59,793
- Now it's a party.
- Cinderella!

671
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,799
So, got a Plan B,
or an extra pair of trousers?

672
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,301
These are the only ones I own.

673
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:11,847
Time to tighten up security here.

674
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:16,268
No one's coming to save you now.

675
00:32:17,853 --> 00:32:20,062
<i>We shouldn't be
out here in the dark.</i>

676
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:21,856
We won't be able to see
if my dad's set another trap.

677
00:32:21,857 --> 00:32:23,482
I'm not taking your advice again.

678
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:26,778
Guys, enough.
He's right. Max threw us way off course.

679
00:32:30,824 --> 00:32:33,200
We need to find a place
to hide out till morning.

680
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:34,910
There's a Lumoria Tree, Red.

681
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,705
It'll keep us safe
from Maddox for the night.

682
00:32:42,294 --> 00:32:44,670
Okay. Anyone want tea?

683
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,924
You're like a little
Wonderland survivalist, aren't ya?

684
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:53,512
I was thinking.

685
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:55,598
How about you, me, and the other HKs

686
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:57,475
take the point heading
to the Palace tomorrow?

687
00:32:58,268 --> 00:32:59,685
I don't trust these VKs.

688
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,729
What are they really
bringing to the table?

689
00:33:01,730 --> 00:33:05,524
<i>Ugh, these hero types
think they own the world.</i>

690
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,902
<i>Time to show 'em VKs can run it.</i>

691
00:33:07,903 --> 00:33:09,696
Not so fast, <i>Senor Hero.</i>

692
00:33:10,614 --> 00:33:14,408
You're gonna need a lot more than good
hair and a nice smile to get this done.

693
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:17,161
<i>You're way more than good hair.</i>

694
00:33:17,162 --> 00:33:19,997
<i>And what does
Hazel Hook know about saving the day?</i>

695
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:22,374
So why don't you leave
the real work to us villains?

696
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:25,878
A Madrigal never
backs down from a challenge.

697
00:33:25,879 --> 00:33:28,047
Go comb your hair, pretty boy.

698
00:33:28,048 --> 00:33:29,548
What are you gonna do? Smile at us?

699
00:33:29,549 --> 00:33:32,801
All right. I've been hearing
a lot of talk from the both of you,

700
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:35,972
but who's really
got what it takes to defeat Maddox? Hmm?

701
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:40,893
You got this.

702
00:33:42,646 --> 00:33:44,438
<i>♪ Listen up ♪</i>

703
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:45,814
<i>♪ I don't mean to flex ♪</i>

704
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:47,441
<i>♪ But let's just be honest ♪</i>

705
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:49,026
<i>♪ Of everyone you met ♪</i>

706
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:50,694
<i>♪ I'm undoubtedly the strongest ♪</i>

707
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:54,073
<i>♪ I got big villain energy
Been scamming since the cradle ♪</i>

708
00:33:54,074 --> 00:33:57,661
<i>♪ From walking planks
to putting chewing gum under your table ♪</i>

709
00:33:58,370 --> 00:34:01,497
<i>♪ The monsters that I fought
are more than just a lot ♪</i>

710
00:34:01,498 --> 00:34:05,334
<i>♪ Once had to put a dragon in a headlock ♪</i>

711
00:34:05,335 --> 00:34:06,669
<i>♪ A pirate in my bones ♪</i>

712
00:34:06,670 --> 00:34:08,337
<i>♪ This hook is solid gold ♪</i>

713
00:34:08,338 --> 00:34:09,964
<i>♪ Believe what you've been told ♪</i>

714
00:34:09,965 --> 00:34:12,091
<i>♪ Did you hear about her? ♪</i>

715
00:34:12,092 --> 00:34:13,634
<i>- ♪ Well, she's a prankster ♪
- Aw!</i>

716
00:34:13,635 --> 00:34:15,511
<i>- ♪ She's a gangster ♪
- That's so sweet.</i>

717
00:34:15,512 --> 00:34:16,679
<i>♪ She's a boss ♪</i>

718
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:19,098
<i>- ♪ Did you hear about him? ♪
- That's me.</i>

719
00:34:19,099 --> 00:34:20,349
<i>♪ He's the greatest ♪</i>

720
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:21,850
<i>♪ Not hard to say this ♪</i>

721
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:23,352
'Cause I'm a fan.

722
00:34:23,353 --> 00:34:25,646
<i>♪ Did you hear about her? ♪</i>

723
00:34:25,647 --> 00:34:27,189
<i>♪ I killed a Kraken ♪</i>

724
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:28,899
<i>♪ With just a napkin ♪</i>

725
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,067
<i>♪ And ate him raw ♪</i>

726
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:32,194
<i>♪ Did you hear about him? ♪</i>

727
00:34:32,195 --> 00:34:33,821
<i>♪ They made a statue ♪</i>

728
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:36,532
<i>♪ I got it tattooed right on my arm ♪</i>

729
00:34:36,533 --> 00:34:38,158
Right here.

730
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:39,493
<i>♪ Did you hear about ♪</i>

731
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:42,663
<i>♪ I mean, no disrespect
but I straight up think you're lying ♪</i>

732
00:34:42,664 --> 00:34:45,916
<i>♪ Someone's overselling
and I'm not sure that I'm buying ♪</i>

733
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,251
<i>♪ I've stopped a cyclone ♪</i>

734
00:34:47,252 --> 00:34:49,169
<i>♪ An avalanche and a tsunami ♪</i>

735
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:51,714
<i>♪ I've tied a giant octopus's
arms like origami ♪</i>

736
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:55,050
<i>♪ A criminal at heart ♪</i>

737
00:34:55,051 --> 00:34:56,635
<i>♪ Each job's a work of art ♪</i>

738
00:34:56,636 --> 00:34:58,012
<i>♪ You're swimming with a shark ♪</i>

739
00:34:58,013 --> 00:35:00,180
<i>♪ Check your pockets ♪</i>

740
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:03,225
<i>♪ I've saved a thousand lives
