1458
01:11:09,891 --> 01:11:12,184
You did this? To my friend?

1459
01:11:12,185 --> 01:11:13,853
How quickly someone's life can change.

1460
01:11:14,979 --> 01:11:15,980
Right?

1461
01:11:16,689 --> 01:11:17,939
Hero to villain.

1462
01:11:17,940 --> 01:11:20,193
A simple flick of the switch or...

1463
01:11:21,444 --> 01:11:22,778
the wind of a watch.

1464
01:11:24,530 --> 01:11:25,531
Yeah.

1465
01:11:26,407 --> 01:11:27,408
That's right.

1466
01:11:28,284 --> 01:11:29,327
I know what you did.

1467
01:11:30,745 --> 01:11:32,872
How you ruined
my chances at a normal life.

1468
01:11:33,372 --> 01:11:34,956
A life that you now have.

1469
01:11:34,957 --> 01:11:36,959
Max, I never meant for that to happen.

1470
01:11:41,047 --> 01:11:42,297
It's time.

1471
01:11:42,298 --> 01:11:43,424
Ominous much?

1472
01:11:44,717 --> 01:11:47,302
Not Princess, just Red, right?

1473
01:11:47,303 --> 01:11:48,596
Maybe I can help with that.

1474
01:11:52,099 --> 01:11:54,185
I'm clearly
out of the loop, but this is bad, right?

1475
01:11:56,562 --> 01:11:57,979
I know what they're after.

1476
01:11:57,980 --> 01:11:59,064
Come on.

1477
01:12:03,486 --> 01:12:04,529
Wait!

1478
01:12:06,781 --> 01:12:08,366
Come on, Red!

1479
01:12:17,625 --> 01:12:18,626
Come on.

1480
01:12:19,585 --> 01:12:21,128
We need to get to the center and fast.

1481
01:12:21,712 --> 01:12:23,171
Oh!

1482
01:12:23,172 --> 01:12:25,675
Okay. How about, um... This way. Yeah.

1483
01:12:29,428 --> 01:12:30,429
I can hear them. This way.

1484
01:12:30,972 --> 01:12:32,472
Whoa! Look out!

1485
01:12:35,977 --> 01:12:37,310
This way.

1486
01:12:37,311 --> 01:12:38,354
Where are they?

1487
01:12:43,818 --> 01:12:45,069
- This way.
- No, wait.

1488
01:12:45,653 --> 01:12:47,113
- But we don't have time--
- Wait!

1489
01:12:48,030 --> 01:12:50,533
Three, two, one.

1490
01:12:59,417 --> 01:13:00,418
Come on.

1491
01:13:01,627 --> 01:13:02,795
Luis, there.

1492
01:13:03,838 --> 01:13:05,338
We'll never make it.

1493
01:13:05,339 --> 01:13:06,715
Yes, you will.

1494
01:13:06,716 --> 01:13:07,924
Go!

1495
01:13:07,925 --> 01:13:09,384
-  What are you doing?
- Hurry!

1496
01:13:09,385 --> 01:13:11,387
I can't hold them off for long. Go!

1497
01:13:12,054 --> 01:13:14,015
Luis!

1498
01:13:14,557 --> 01:13:16,141
No!

1499
01:13:16,142 --> 01:13:18,519
I'll find you. I promise.

1500
01:13:19,145 --> 01:13:20,270
No, no, no, no.

1501
01:13:25,484 --> 01:13:26,568
Chloe?

1502
01:13:26,569 --> 01:13:27,820
Max, keep up.

1503
01:13:30,615 --> 01:13:32,158
Chloe?

1504
01:13:33,200 --> 01:13:34,201
Where are you?

1505
01:13:35,703 --> 01:13:36,954
<i>Selfish.</i>

1506
01:13:38,706 --> 01:13:39,916
<i>Ruthless.</i>

1507
01:13:42,084 --> 01:13:43,586
<i>Ruined my life.</i>

1508
01:13:45,671 --> 01:13:46,923
<i>Hard to love.</i>

1509
01:13:48,174 --> 01:13:50,175
<i>You're such a disappointment.</i>

1510
01:13:50,176 --> 01:13:51,677
Hearing things?

1511
01:13:52,386 --> 01:13:54,930
Warmer. Warmer.

1512
01:13:54,931 --> 01:13:57,557
Unlike them, I'm not in your head.

1513
01:13:57,558 --> 01:13:59,309
Chessy, leave me alone.

1514
01:13:59,310 --> 01:14:02,229
Not exactly crushing
this whole hero thing, huh?

1515
01:14:02,939 --> 01:14:04,898
I never asked for this.

1516
01:14:04,899 --> 01:14:06,484
Except you kinda did.

1517
01:14:07,485 --> 01:14:09,110
Now they all hate me.

1518
01:14:09,111 --> 01:14:11,446
Well, you did ruin the Hatters' lives,

1519
01:14:11,447 --> 01:14:12,822
got your mom captured,

1520
01:14:12,823 --> 01:14:15,408
left your boyfriend
in a shrub, and, oh, yeah,

1521
01:14:15,409 --> 01:14:18,037
nearly fed your bestie
to a bloodthirsty flower.

1522
01:14:18,996 --> 01:14:22,458
Didn't exactly
figure it out together, did you?

1523
01:14:23,542 --> 01:14:24,918
Leave me alone.

1524
01:14:33,260 --> 01:14:35,762
<i>♪ I'm so lost and defeated ♪</i>

1525
01:14:35,763 --> 01:14:40,058
<i>♪ I've been climbing
but I keep getting knocked down ♪</i>

1526
01:14:40,059 --> 01:14:42,937
<i>♪ Down, down, down ♪</i>

1527
01:14:44,563 --> 01:14:47,315
<i>♪ How can a villain be a hero? ♪</i>

1528
01:14:47,316 --> 01:14:51,611
<i>♪ I don't even seem to recognize me now ♪</i>

1529
01:14:51,612 --> 01:14:54,407
<i>♪ Now ♪</i>

1530
01:14:56,200 --> 01:14:59,619
<i>♪ Every mistake's led me here ♪</i>

1531
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:04,166
<i>♪ Now it's all up to me ♪</i>

1532
01:15:07,628 --> 01:15:12,341
<i>♪ Will I ever know who I am? ♪</i>

1533
01:15:13,259 --> 01:15:18,222
<i>♪ Will I ever get the chance? ♪</i>

1534
01:15:19,390 --> 01:15:24,853
<i>♪ Can I find the strength
that's deep inside me ♪</i>

1535
01:15:24,854 --> 01:15:29,566
<i>♪ Will ever understand ♪</i>

1536
01:15:29,567 --> 01:15:31,484
<i>♪ Who I am? ♪</i>

1537
01:15:31,485 --> 01:15:34,279
<i>♪ I made a mess and now my... ♪</i>

1538
01:15:34,280 --> 01:15:36,531
<i>♪ My time is running out ♪</i>

1539
01:15:36,532 --> 01:15:40,369
<i>♪ There's no second chances this time ♪</i>

1540
01:15:40,995 --> 01:15:42,954
<i>♪ No, whoa ♪</i>

1541
01:15:42,955 --> 01:15:45,165
<i>♪ This rebel deep inside ♪</i>

1542
01:15:45,166 --> 01:15:48,043
<i>♪ Won't go down without a fight ♪</i>

1543
01:15:48,044 --> 01:15:53,340
<i>♪ Won't give up till I make this right! ♪</i>

1544
01:16:42,056 --> 01:16:43,057
Pink!

1545
01:16:44,183 --> 01:16:45,975
Pink, I need you.

1546
01:16:45,976 --> 01:16:47,311
-  Pink!
- Red?

1547
01:16:49,146 --> 01:16:52,191
That's my sister in there,
and she needs me.

1548
01:16:52,775 --> 01:16:54,526
Open up this instant!

1549
01:16:56,320 --> 01:16:58,114
Oh. Thanks.

1550
01:17:02,243 --> 01:17:03,244
Red.

1551
01:17:07,665 --> 01:17:08,748
You came.

1552
01:17:08,749 --> 01:17:09,750
Of course.

1553
01:17:10,251 --> 01:17:11,835
That's what sisters do.

1554
01:17:14,338 --> 01:17:15,631
Where did you find that?

1555
01:17:16,549 --> 01:17:18,134
I remembered we left it here.

1556
01:17:22,429 --> 01:17:25,306
<i>♪ Now I know who I am ♪</i>

1557
01:17:25,307 --> 01:17:28,017
<i>♪ Who I am ♪</i>

1558
01:17:28,018 --> 01:17:32,272
<i>♪ I finally have the chance ♪</i>

1559
01:17:32,273 --> 01:17:34,065
<i>♪ Have the chance ♪</i>

1560
01:17:34,066 --> 01:17:39,696
<i>♪ I can feel
the strength that's deep inside me ♪</i>

1561
01:17:39,697 --> 01:17:44,242
<i>♪ Now I understand ♪</i>

1562
01:17:44,243 --> 01:17:46,787
<i>♪ Who I am ♪</i>

1563
01:17:48,956 --> 01:17:50,999
Pink, please tell me you still have

1564
01:17:51,000 --> 01:17:53,334
some of those cookies
left from the picnic.

1565
01:17:53,335 --> 01:17:54,336
Sure do.

1566
01:18:06,056 --> 01:18:08,767
Who's the big sister now?

1567
01:18:11,020 --> 01:18:12,103
Come on, Maddox.

1568
01:18:12,104 --> 01:18:13,730
- Just let us out.
- Please.

1569
01:18:13,731 --> 01:18:14,856
Think about your son.

1570
01:18:14,857 --> 01:18:16,649
Hmm.

1571
01:18:16,650 --> 01:18:19,360
Should've brought a bigger broom.

1572
01:18:19,361 --> 01:18:21,404
Time's up, Queens.

1573
01:18:21,405 --> 01:18:24,199
The pocket watch is nearly mine.

1574
01:18:25,409 --> 01:18:27,745
I'm so proud of you, Max!

1575
01:18:53,520 --> 01:18:54,521
Finally.

1576
01:18:55,606 --> 01:18:56,607
For my father.

1577
01:18:57,107 --> 01:18:58,484
For the life we could've had.

1578
01:18:59,026 --> 01:19:01,611
- For Red's betrayal.
- And my revenge.

1579
01:19:03,405 --> 01:19:04,406
Hey, guys.

1580
01:19:05,199 --> 01:19:06,282
Miss us?

1581
01:19:06,283 --> 01:19:07,701
Us?

1582
01:19:09,203 --> 01:19:10,745
Hi!

1583
01:19:23,509 --> 01:19:25,135
Red, are you okay?

1584
01:19:25,928 --> 01:19:27,011
Go, Pink.

1585
01:19:27,012 --> 01:19:28,263
Get the others.

1586
01:19:28,264 --> 01:19:30,848
Okay.

1587
01:19:30,849 --> 01:19:31,850
Where is it?

1588
01:19:32,601 --> 01:19:34,061
Where's the pocket watch?

1589
01:19:42,903 --> 01:19:44,280
Chloe...

1590
01:19:47,157 --> 01:19:48,701
Think about what you're doing.

1591
01:19:49,451 --> 01:19:50,494
This isn't you.

1592
01:19:51,078 --> 01:19:52,746
Weren't you listening, Red?

1593
01:19:53,747 --> 01:19:56,124
Of course it's not me.

1594
01:19:56,125 --> 01:19:57,668
Not the me that you knew, anyway.

1595
01:19:58,419 --> 01:19:59,794
No.

1596
01:19:59,795 --> 01:20:02,505
I'm free of her.

1597
01:20:02,506 --> 01:20:04,215
So click the dial, Chloe.

1598
01:20:04,216 --> 01:20:05,842
Our pain will disappear.

1599
01:20:05,843 --> 01:20:08,761
It'll all go away,
and she will be the one left hurting.

1600
01:20:08,762 --> 01:20:10,389
It's the perfect revenge.

1601
01:20:10,931 --> 01:20:13,017
Put our lives back the way they were.

1602
01:20:14,893 --> 01:20:15,977
Do it.

1603
01:20:17,521 --> 01:20:20,189
You think I'm doing this for you, Max?

1604
01:20:20,190 --> 01:20:21,733
Or your dad?

1605
01:20:23,319 --> 01:20:24,777
Aw.

1606
01:20:24,778 --> 01:20:26,821
No, I... I've seen the past.

1607
01:20:26,822 --> 01:20:29,615
I've seen that sad story.

1608
01:20:29,616 --> 01:20:32,661
No, I say we turn this around
and look to the future.

1609
01:20:34,413 --> 01:20:37,707
A future where I'll finally be on top,

1610
01:20:37,708 --> 01:20:39,000
and you'll know what it's like

1611
01:20:39,001 --> 01:20:41,044
to feel invisible and pushed aside.

1612
01:20:41,045 --> 01:20:43,629
A future where I won't need either of you.

1613
01:20:43,630 --> 01:20:45,715
- But I gave you that power.
- And I took it.

1614
01:20:45,716 --> 01:20:47,050
Chloe, you were right.

1615
01:20:47,051 --> 01:20:48,594
About everything.

1616
01:20:50,220 --> 01:20:51,388
Traveling to the past,

1617
01:20:51,930 --> 01:20:53,390
going back to save your mom,

1618
01:20:54,475 --> 01:20:55,684
changed my life.

1619
01:20:57,061 --> 01:20:59,645
I finally knew
what it was to do something good.

1620
01:20:59,646 --> 01:21:01,689
And that's because you believed in me.

1621
01:21:01,690 --> 01:21:04,651
You showed me that I wasn't a lost cause.

1622
01:21:05,361 --> 01:21:07,988
You had my back every single time.

1623
01:21:09,073 --> 01:21:11,658
I know these last few days
I haven't had yours.

1624
01:21:13,118 --> 01:21:14,119
But I do now.

1625
01:21:15,496 --> 01:21:16,622
I believe in you.

1626
01:21:17,831 --> 01:21:18,832
In us.

1627
01:21:21,418 --> 01:21:22,503
If you do this,

1628
01:21:23,295 --> 01:21:24,463
we lose everything.

1629
01:21:27,049 --> 01:21:28,633
We lose each other.

1630
01:21:30,260 --> 01:21:31,803
No, don't listen to her, Chloe.

1631
01:21:31,804 --> 01:21:33,514
Enough! Both of you!

1632
01:21:37,309 --> 01:21:38,726
<i>♪ We'll figure it out ♪</i>

1633
01:21:38,727 --> 01:21:40,687
<i>♪ Figure it out together ♪</i>

1634
01:21:42,648 --> 01:21:45,734
<i>♪ Figure it out
Figure it out together ♪</i>

1635
01:21:51,490 --> 01:21:52,615
<i>♪ Figure it out ♪</i>

1636
01:21:52,616 --> 01:21:55,119
<i>♪ Figure it out together ♪</i>

1637
01:22:07,965 --> 01:22:08,966
Chloe!

1638
01:22:12,136 --> 01:22:13,302
No!

1639
01:22:15,139 --> 01:22:17,056
This is your midnight, Maddox.

1640
01:22:17,057 --> 01:22:18,224
Time to go.

1641
01:22:19,643 --> 01:22:22,228
Ace for effort, though.
You really did give it your all.

1642
01:22:25,232 --> 01:22:26,315
Maddox--

1643
01:22:26,316 --> 01:22:27,776
We'll see who gets
the last laugh.

1644
01:22:32,906 --> 01:22:34,198
Oh, no.

1645
01:22:34,199 --> 01:22:35,284
No!

1646
01:22:36,368 --> 01:22:37,786
The watch!

1647
01:22:39,163 --> 01:22:40,663
It's mine.

1648
01:22:44,376 --> 01:22:45,668
Max, look out!

1649
01:22:49,631 --> 01:22:51,008
Please!

1650
01:22:54,511 --> 01:22:55,761
Together on three. Ready?

1651
01:22:55,762 --> 01:22:57,263
One, two, three!

1652
01:22:57,264 --> 01:22:58,723
It's gonna fall!

1653
01:22:58,724 --> 01:22:59,725
No, no, no!

1654
01:23:05,022 --> 01:23:06,481
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

1655
01:23:19,119 --> 01:23:20,120
Thank you.

1656
01:23:22,206 --> 01:23:23,540
What about the watch?

1657
01:23:32,174 --> 01:23:33,342
What do we do with it now?

1658
01:23:36,261 --> 01:23:38,514
I'm sorry, Max, but we can't go back.

1659
01:23:39,848 --> 01:23:42,392
This has caused all of us enough pain.

1660
01:23:45,437 --> 01:23:47,522
Will you still try and help my father?

1661
01:23:47,523 --> 01:23:49,691
I won't abandon you or your dad.

1662
01:23:50,567 --> 01:23:51,652
I promise.

1663
01:24:12,923 --> 01:24:14,382
<i>The pocket watch.</i>

1664
01:24:14,383 --> 01:24:15,967
No!

1665
01:24:15,968 --> 01:24:17,510
I will destroy Wonderland!

1666
01:24:17,511 --> 01:24:19,845
-  Come on, let's go!
-  Thanks, Pink!

1667
01:24:19,846 --> 01:24:21,597
Knock knock.

1668
01:24:21,598 --> 01:24:22,682
Pink?

1669
01:24:22,683 --> 01:24:24,184
What in the hat?

1670
01:24:25,894 --> 01:24:27,270
Oh! Get him!

1671
01:24:27,271 --> 01:24:28,981
A-ha! There.

1672
01:24:30,440 --> 01:24:32,192
- Over here!
- Hook!

1673
01:24:34,528 --> 01:24:35,654
Now.

1674
01:24:40,784 --> 01:24:42,535
We did it!

1675
01:24:42,536 --> 01:24:44,036
Top that, Hatter!

1676
01:24:44,037 --> 01:24:45,538
You're not going anywhere, Hatter!

1677
01:24:47,332 --> 01:24:49,000
Oh, someone's stuck.

1678
01:24:49,001 --> 01:24:50,502
Not bad for a pirate.

1679
01:24:51,044 --> 01:24:53,629
Look at you.
Hair still perfectly in place.

1680
01:24:53,630 --> 01:24:54,964
Heh. It's a talent.

1681
01:25:07,144 --> 01:25:09,520
I missed you. I missed you, and you--

1682
01:25:09,521 --> 01:25:10,522
Mom.

1683
01:25:11,481 --> 01:25:12,565
- My darling.
- Mom?

1684
01:25:12,566 --> 01:25:14,734
Ah. Red.

1685
01:25:15,986 --> 01:25:17,111
Dad.

1686
01:25:17,112 --> 01:25:18,571
Oh, I'm so happy to see you.

1687
01:25:18,572 --> 01:25:19,573
Hmm.

1688
01:25:20,365 --> 01:25:22,742
- You're okay.
- Yes. Are you?

1689
01:25:22,743 --> 01:25:23,826
Uh, yeah.

1690
01:25:23,827 --> 01:25:25,537
- I missed you.
- Oh, honey.

1691
01:25:26,747 --> 01:25:29,081
-  I like the pants.
- Me too.

1692
01:25:32,753 --> 01:25:35,171
- I can't believe you made it.
- Hey, guys.

1693
01:25:35,172 --> 01:25:37,048
Pink saved us with cookies.

1694
01:25:37,049 --> 01:25:38,507
-  You all right?
-  Yeah.

1695
01:25:38,508 --> 01:25:41,136
How dare you come into my palace,

1696
01:25:42,262 --> 01:25:44,431
endanger my children,

1697
01:25:44,931 --> 01:25:47,850
and use my magic against me?

1698
01:25:47,851 --> 01:25:51,228
Off with his head!

1699
01:25:55,567 --> 01:25:58,819
Where in heavens
did that come from?

1700
01:25:58,820 --> 01:26:01,572
Guards. Take him away.

1701
01:26:01,573 --> 01:26:03,575
-  No, Dad.
- Stop. You can't.

1702
01:26:04,076 --> 01:26:05,285
This is all my fault.

1703
01:26:07,162 --> 01:26:08,163
It's true, Mom.

1704
01:26:10,040 --> 01:26:12,125
Maddox, I'm sorry about everything.

1705
01:26:15,587 --> 01:26:17,338
This all started because I was too afraid

1706
01:26:17,339 --> 01:26:18,757
to stand up for what was right.

1707
01:26:19,716 --> 01:26:21,134
Too afraid to disappoint you.

1708
01:26:22,177 --> 01:26:23,804
Then, and now.

1709
01:26:25,138 --> 01:26:26,640
I'm no hero, Mom.

1710
01:26:27,891 --> 01:26:30,686
It's what a person does that defines them.

1711
01:26:31,603 --> 01:26:33,188
Hero?

1712
01:26:33,730 --> 01:26:35,065
That's just a word.

1713
01:26:36,733 --> 01:26:37,734
Then...

1714
01:26:39,194 --> 01:26:40,445
maybe so is villain.

1715
01:26:41,947 --> 01:26:43,699
Maybe everyone deserves a do-over.

1716
01:26:48,870 --> 01:26:50,622
He can keep his head.

1717
01:26:51,790 --> 01:26:53,290
Hm.

1718
01:26:53,291 --> 01:26:57,671
But he can also
stay cozy in there for a little bit.

1719
01:27:02,634 --> 01:27:04,302
So I heard you have a dark side.

1720
01:27:04,928 --> 01:27:06,637
Nice.

1721
01:27:06,638 --> 01:27:08,223
Maybe I was wrong about you.

